From b0a046a9e13bdce9ddbf836e138d54ebe65355ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:03:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(ui): preview the incoming stock in the viewport on
 the setup page

While a setup's settings page is open and its stock source is "What
<previous setup> leaves behind", the viewport draws the body the setups
before it leave (stock_sim::incoming_body's display sheet) as a teal
translucent stock-slot part, apart from the setup's own Stock node.

- app: setup_stock_view::incoming_shape measures the incoming body once
  (box, volume and the sheet as triangles), carried into the active
  setup's frame (A_active * A_setup^-1; identity when the setup is the
  active one).
- ui: incoming_view caches it in State keyed by (setup, active setup,
  doc_version), refreshed at the end of drain_actions; it measures only
  when the key moves and drops the mesh the moment the page closes,
  another page opens or the setup takes its own stock. The page's box
  and volume read the same measurement (one program sim per version).
- viewport: fs_stock paints class 4 as the incoming-stock teal.

A refusal draws nothing, is logged once per measurement and stays on
the page as before. View state only - no command, nothing undoable.

Fixes #406

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
